    {
      "week": 48,
      "slug": "inside-outside-covers",
      "title": "Inside and outside covers",
      "idea": "Inside and covering tiles certify area bounds; refinement tightens them while a coarse certificate can hide different areas.",
      "gates": "K-1: distinguish whole, partial and outside cells with adult counting. Older bands: regroup four small squares into one big square, then compare bounds. Fractions are optional; exact area formulas are unnecessary.",
      "materials": "Actual-size 120 mm mats, paper 30 mm and 15 mm squares, tracing paper or transparent sleeves and pencils. Shade larger fine covers instead of making many loose tiles.",
      "pretest": "Measure print and tile fit before use; physical tests are unperformed. Keep the big-square unit fixed and demonstrate that edge-only or corner-only touching adds no cover cell.",
