    {
      "week": 49,
      "slug": "four-tower-differences",
      "title": "Four towers and differences",
      "idea": "Simultaneous neighboring differences always send four nonnegative integer towers to zero, through a bound and increasing divisibility.",
      "gates": "K-1: match towers to find the unmatched part, with adult recording. Grades 2-3: small absolute differences. Grades 4-5: parity and repeated scaling; the final universal proof is optional after concrete exploration.",
      "materials": "Separate labeled old/new mats, number cards or erasable markers and optional cubes. Working stations are 40 mm squares; small printed rings are reference diagrams.",
      "pretest": "Rehearse a complete simultaneous update before swapping mats. Keep all four old heights unchanged until every new value is ready. Cube fit and classroom handling remain untested.",
