    {
      "week": 50,
      "slug": "staircases-and-lengths",
      "title": "Staircases and lengths",
      "idea": "Right-up staircases can approach a diagonal while their length stays fixed; backtracking and corridor constraints expose different quantities.",
      "gates": "K-1: right/up directions and side-by-side length comparisons. Grades 2-3: add segment lengths. Grades 4-5: control a vertical-gap constraint and distinguish positional approximation from length. Square-root derivation is unnecessary.",
      "materials": "Nonstretch strings, rulers, pencils and removable tape. Main rectangles are 160 by 120 mm; the smaller guide diagram is not a measuring mat.",
      "pretest": "Check the printed 100 mm calibration, string stretch and corner-following before teaching. These physical tests are unperformed. The corridor uses vertical gap, not perpendicular distance.",
