    {
      "week": 51,
      "slug": "honest-measurement-ranges",
      "title": "Honest measurement ranges",
      "idea": "Endpoint witnesses prove sharp sum and difference guarantees; shared pieces and exact totals reveal dependencies.",
      "gates": "K-1: match endpoints and count small lengths with adult reading. Grades 2-3: add, subtract and compare intervals. Grades 4-5: track repeated quantities and constrained totals. Negative numbers are unnecessary in these tasks.",
      "materials": "Sliding paper strips, opaque sleeves or a cover card, rulers and exact white add-ons. One unit is 10 mm; main 0-16 rulers span 160 mm. Repeated A must have the same length in both uses.",
      "pretest": "Measure actual scale and rehearse sliding, hiding and reusing the same A; tests remain unperformed. Cards stipulate guaranteed bounds, including endpoints, without claiming a measured instrument-error distribution.",
